# Patch series. Every entry must match a patches/<id>.patch file whose SHA256
# matches, and every patches/*.patch must be declared here (checked on every
# pull request by build/checks/patch_integrity.sh and build/checks/
# manifest_schema.sh). Updates are reviewed pull requests only (rule 13.4).
patches:
  - id: "0100"
    name: SukiSU-Nova driver integration (drivers/kernelsu wiring)
    description: >-
      Wires the pinned SukiSU-Nova tree into the kernel build as a built-in
      driver (route A): registers drivers/kernelsu in drivers/Makefile and
      sources its Kconfig from drivers/Kconfig. Equivalent to the Makefile and
      Kconfig edits SukiSU-Nova's kernel/setup.sh performs at commit
      c60f21b9, re-recorded as a reviewed patch. The drivers/kernelsu symlink
      into the pinned submodule is created at build time by
      build/integrate_sukisu.sh (setup.sh's git clone/pull is never executed,
      project rule 13.4.2).
    source_url: https://github.com/SukiSU-Nova/SukiSU-Nova
    upstream_commit: c60f21b9e00e35e898f8d21e0612465b76b9beec
    sha256: 9399ff47e11121e252d253588b93eeca7ff10689598e96a48bee149229a5a8ea
    license: GPL-3.0-or-later
  - id: "0200"
    name: Drop Kconfig sources for the unpublished kernel/oplus_cpu trees
    description: >-
      The published OnePlusOSS tree sources kernel/oplus_cpu/*/Kconfig
      (cpufreq_health, uad, oplus_omrg, cpufreq_bouncing, oplus_overload,
      waker_identify) from drivers/soc/Kconfig and kernel/oplus_cpu/sched/Kconfig
      from init/Kconfig, but the kernel/oplus_cpu directory is not part of the
      OSS release, so stock kconfig aborts with 'can't open file'. The guarded
      blocks are removed. CONFIG_OPLUS_FEATURE_PERFORMANCE_SCHED is kept off in
      the build profiles because kernel/Makefile builds oplus_cpu/sched/ from
      it and that directory is likewise unpublished.
    source_url: https://github.com/OnePlusOSS/android_kernel_oneplus_sm8650
    upstream_commit: b2696d4a2bda11cb74de35f839ef0cf6ccc1b9cb
    sha256: 5806a720b8cd6dd37d8a9e215c873cb022c0a56ea966daaa42b8ac4c547d1190
    license: GPL-2.0-only
  - id: "0210"
    name: Drop the mm/mm_osvelte source from mm/Kconfig
    description: >-
      mm/Kconfig sources mm/mm_osvelte/Kconfig, but mm/mm_osvelte is published
      as a single file, not a directory, so stock kconfig aborts with
      'mm/Kconfig:1313: can't open file'. The source line is removed; the
      CONFIG_MM_OSVELTE symbol is undefined afterwards and mm/Makefile's
      obj- mapping for mm_osvelte.o therefore stays inert.
    source_url: https://github.com/OnePlusOSS/android_kernel_oneplus_sm8650
    upstream_commit: b2696d4a2bda11cb74de35f839ef0cf6ccc1b9cb
    sha256: ebd81474a3371bde7fc4b76c24139ff86ea21a5c43698226f7b1b31e78e1293a
    license: GPL-2.0-only
  - id: "0220"
    name: Drop remaining missing-source references from five subsystem Kconfigs
    description: >-
      A full audit of all Kconfig files at the pinned OnePlusOSS commit found
      21 remaining `source` lines pointing at files that are not part of the
      OSS release (the OPLUS feature Kconfigs were stripped from the published
      tree even where the driver source directories remain): drivers/base
      (kernelFwUpdate, touchpanel_notify), drivers/iio/stm/imu (st_asm330lhhx),
      drivers/misc/vibrator (aw8697_haptic, si_haptic, oplus_haptic),
      drivers/power (oplus) and drivers/soc (the drivers/soc/oplus features
      plus their boot/storage/power sub-features). Removing the source lines
      lets stock kconfig finish; the corresponding CONFIG_* symbols then stay
      undefined and their obj- mappings remain inert. Completes the cleanup
      started by patches 0200 and 0210.
    source_url: https://github.com/OnePlusOSS/android_kernel_oneplus_sm8650
    upstream_commit: b2696d4a2bda11cb74de35f839ef0cf6ccc1b9cb
    sha256: 33f549ad3ddaae9819d454c955c9c8528ae1942a631f7561e22b26cf50f35a6c
    license: GPL-2.0-only
  - id: "0230"
    name: Guard the unguarded oplus_cpu uses in kernel/sched/walt/walt_halt.c
    description: >-
      walt_halt.c uses oplus_cur_pause_client, cur_cpus_halt_mask,
      cur_cpus_phalt_mask and sa_corectl_systrace_c unconditionally inside
      CONFIG_HOTPLUG_CPU, while their declarations are published only behind
      the oplus_cpu include guards, so the OSS tree does not compile with those
      features off. The five use sites are wrapped in
      #if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_OPLUS_FEATURE_SCHED_ASSIST) so the file compiles
      both ways. Verified against the pinned file (git apply --check clean).
    source_url: https://github.com/OnePlusOSS/android_kernel_oneplus_sm8650
    upstream_commit: b2696d4a2bda11cb74de35f839ef0cf6ccc1b9cb
    sha256: 118d0c66477a483c5a92d66c81d04fd66ad1686017007843c255b403684df6d8
    license: GPL-2.0-only


  - id: "0240"
    name: Drop unconditional obj-y entries into the unpublished oplus trees
    description: >-
      kernel/locking/Makefile lists oplus_locking.o in an unconditional obj-y,
      and drivers/soc/Makefile lists oplus/boot/, oplus/dft/ and oplus/storage/
      in obj-y lines that sit inside '#ifdef OPLUS_FEATURE_*' blocks. kbuild
      treats such blocks as comments, so those references are unconditional,
      while the four targets exist only behind symlinks into trees that are
      not part of the OSS release, which is why stock make aborts with
      "No rule to make target 'kernel/locking/oplus_locking.o'". The four
      obj-y entries are removed; every remaining oplus reference in both
      Makefiles is obj-$(CONFIG_...) and inert, because patches 0200/0210/0220
      removed the Kconfig sources that defined their symbols.
    source_url: https://github.com/OnePlusOSS/android_kernel_oneplus_sm8650
    upstream_commit: b2696d4a2bda11cb74de35f839ef0cf6ccc1b9cb
    sha256: 1ea5526994cebc9cf470346420e5e9114cf570fcc42d63ab4d83155000413d6a
    license: GPL-2.0-only